<section class="tiny-architecture" aria-labelledby="transformer-architecture">
  <header>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Decoder-only Transformer · report design</p>
      <h2 id="transformer-architecture">The architecture, tensor by tensor.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      BPE converts text into token IDs. Each position becomes a vector, gathers
      information from earlier tokens, and predicts the next token.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div
    class="architecture-settings"
    aria-label="Configuration specified by the training script"
  >
    <span>
      <strong>3,000</strong> vocabulary entries
    </span>
    <span>
      <strong>256</strong> context / embedding width
    </span>
    <span>
      <strong>5</strong> decoder blocks
    </span>
    <span>
      <strong>8 × 32</strong> attention heads × dimensions
    </span>
  </div>
  <figure>
    <a
      href="/media/tinystories/architecture.svg"
      aria-label="Enlarge the Transformer tensor flow"
    >
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(max-width: 700px)"
          srcset="/media/tinystories/architecture-mobile.svg"
        />
        <img
          src="/media/tinystories/architecture.svg"
          width="1180"
          height="300"
          alt="Token IDs select rows of the learned embedding table E. Position vectors are added; five decoder blocks preserve T by 256 shape. Final LayerNorm and the tied E transpose projection produce T by 3000 logits."
        />
      </picture>
    </a>
    <figcaption>
      One sequence; T is its length. Each colored row is a token vector. Colors
      are schematic, not saved weights. The output reuses the embedding matrix
      E.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure class="block-figure">
    <div class="block-heading">
      <h3>Inside a decoder block</h3>
      <span>Same structure repeated 5 times</span>
    </div>
    <a
      href="/media/tinystories/decoder-block.svg"
      aria-label="Enlarge the pre-norm attention and feed-forward block"
    >
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(max-width: 700px)"
          srcset="/media/tinystories/decoder-block-mobile.svg"
        />
        <img
          src="/media/tinystories/decoder-block.svg"
          width="1180"
          height="290"
          alt="LayerNorm precedes attention. Q and K determine causal attention scores; V supplies content. Eight heads are concatenated and projected before a residual addition. A second LayerNorm and feed-forward network, 256 to 384 to 256, precede another residual addition."
        />
      </picture>
    </a>
    <figcaption>
      The causal mask blocks future positions; residual paths preserve
      information and gradient flow. Pre-norm follows the homework description;
      dimensions follow the configured design.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="training-objective">
    <span class="loop" aria-hidden="true">
      ↺
    </span>
    <p>
      <strong>Learning:</strong> logits + targets shifted by one token →
      cross-entropy → backpropagation → AdamW.{' '}
      <span>
        Batch 8 · learning rate 5 × 10<sup>−5</sup> · gradient norm capped at 1.
      </span>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="architecture-status">
    The local model file overrides this design with an embedding-only prototype.
    The diagrams describe the intended Transformer; they do not establish the
    architecture used for the reported run.{' '}
    <a href="#implementation-evidence">Source notes ↓</a>
  </p>
</section>

